readme.text:
- read the task, acceptance criteria, tests and relevant code before editing; reproduce the failure and name the
  root cause as `file:line` first;
- make the smallest change, keep public interfaces, no unrelated refactors or formatting churn;
- never edit, delete, weaken, skip or xfail tests, and never hardcode expected values;
- ground every API, import and parameter in the repository or installed dependencies before using it;
- run the repository's real verification command after the last edit and iterate until it passes;
- verify only from the repository's own spec/tests/code — do not speculate about hidden tests, graders or
  benchmarks, and do not read parent/sibling directories or git history for hints;
- for specs with more than ~15 numbered acceptance clauses, keep a clause → implementation → verification
  checklist; for performance/concurrency work, report measured evidence once instead of re-running stress loops;
- end with evidence: files changed, root cause, exact commands with observed results, unverified parts, risks.

- solved rate was identical (15/16 vs 15/16; the single failure was one ambiguous hidden-test assertion that
  both arms failed in one seed and passed in another);
- injected instructions were observed in 18/18 enhanced runs and the skill was loaded in 18/18; no run tampered
  with tests or read outside its working directory;
- token usage and wall-clock differences were not statistically significant — run-to-run variance dominated.
